 and creativity in  every conceivable scenario i mean  during this chase scene in order to not  slow down when approaching civilians at  a crosswalk he destroys his bike  leaps through the air with the parts  flying through the air and then  reassembles the motorbike before landing  again without any  loss of speed like that's such a cool  visually interesting thing and  a fun idea that makes use of his power  this chase is by far the highlight of  this two-part episode and josuke  eventually locates where the stand user  was staying after some investigation and  quick thinking on behalf of koichi that  points josuke to the room of the  hospital that he finds the stand user  apparently he's been sucking nutrients  to try to heal himself  and in retaliation for everything that  he's put josuke through josuke heals him  and beats the hell out of him returning  him to his once debilitated state  it's quite funny okay so let's talk  about kira interestingly instead of the  first half of the story which heavily  focused on  and concerned itself with the slice of  life character interactions and  exploration into the town of mario this  second half has the constant presence of  kira informing pretty much every episode  and the audience once again  are made aware of kira's new persona  giving us that extra layer of dramatic  irony the main cast aren't aware of yet  as we follow kira as he explores his new  world  and family for the first time and in an  ironic twist of fate  the one stale relationship on the verge  of collapse kira's host once had  now seems to be a much better fit for  him as a personality with his new wife's  romantic interests rekindled and at a  new all-time high and their financial  trouble is seemingly on the mend  thanks exclusively to kiera's choices as  an individual the scenes that he  participates in early on are clearly  there to give him something to struggle  against or bounce off of while the  others are trying to find him and work  their way towards the finale in other  words the hero team and the evil squad  are both sort of in this waiting phase  before they've reached the climax of  this story the first of these mini  adventures with the new keator concerns  a particular cat that his wife  accidentally kills and he buries in the  back garden the cat once possessing a  stand now has sprouted as a flower a  cat flower if you will this also  explains all of the suggestions i  received to name my bonsai stray cat  this manifestation of a cat flower  stand user that can shoot high-speed air  bubbles that can cause serious damage  are quickly taken care of by cure by way  of hiding it from light in his attic  now this brings me to the last and final  aspect of the story that i otherwise  didn't really buy  into and that's their son hayato  kawagiri you see while kira was  pondering to himself concerning his  current state of affairs and worries  out loud while practicing the  handwriting of his new host  the kid didn't just hear him but he was  filming him and this  isn't the only time this kid sets up spy  equipment either now  this criticism i have might very well be  the result of my growing up in an  otherwise rural part of the world  or it might be the fact that iraqi  thought the world would be much more  technologically advanced by the turn of  the millennium but  for a kid to have all of this genuinely  impressive spy equipment  seems really far-fetched to me and not  just that the fact that this kid has  surveillance over his father so  effectively  is essentially the only reason kira gets  found out at all in the end  every subsequent clue or connected dot  the gang unraveled during their  investigation only manifests uncertainty  because of the child's suspicions of his  father that came from these hidden  camera setups  alright okay that's everything i didn't  like so let's talk about something what  i did like  episodes 31 32 33 and 34.  so yoshihiro kira's father by random  happenstance notices and identifies his  son kira by looking at his fingernails  why okay so the hook of these episodes  is that they are all taking place on  essentially the same day july 15  1999. rohan takes a picture at the exact  same time hayato is investigating his  father giving him means with which to  learn his name because  his school bag has a surname on it and  josuke and okay to defeat another stand  user in the transmission tower thanks to  mr  alien man kayak are the buckets  transmission tower man reveals that  koichi has been eliminated and  in order to track down the dude that  took out koichi josuke implies the help  of someone he knows that has a great  sense of smell  and wide range stand this guy remember  him i do  and he finds him the gentleman that they  were searching down had stands that in  all honesty were  not at all anything that i would have  expected he can apparently suck people  into pieces of paper if they are scared  and he's already got koichi so  now he's sucky in josuke i love that  josuke hangs on to something from the  outside world and despite being sucked  into the i don't know  origami dimension using his crazy  diamond he manages to restore what he  was holding and thus momentarily drags  himself  out while this didn't work i once again  thought it was a super cool idea to  combine these two powers and what it  might manifest as thankfully however for  josuke and koichi for that matter they  are released after the guy that smells  good  saves them in a really creative way the  following episode episode 34 kind of  bugs me but  once again made rohan my favorite  character from this part  alright so he sort of gets this back  gremlin stand stuck  onto him and okay i know it's creepy and  all that stuff but  what bugged me about it wasn't the stand  or anything like that it was the fact  that when he reached out to koichi for  help  koichi didn't believe him i mean come on  man you're now living in a world with  stand magic an evil stand 