ve of kira early on it helps to  put us into his shoes not to empathize  with him necessarily but to instead  feel the strains and pressures he feels  as people in his life skirt around and  press the lines of truth in his  character  causing him great anxiety fearing his  identity being exposed  there's a clearly observed almost  pathetic and desperate nature to cure  his character  particularly after his new son discovers  the truth about him and outs it to him  which i found in later encounters helps  to add a separate perspective in battles  to keep an eye on no longer are we  looking at villains that always seem to  be in control  kira's character's entertainment factor  largely comes from how he reacts to bad  news  and like the heroes struggles to make  sense of situations trying to solve  problems that present themselves in real  time with jotaro and josuke hot on his  tail  in this state of terror and anxiety over  being found out his father tries to calm  him down  when suddenly the same arrow that sought  out all of those other stand users  forces itself from the photograph and  into kira's body  before cutting to black from the depths  of this seemingly irreversibly  impossible to escape from scenario  came the following day now completely  calm and  brandishing a brand new hairstyle stands  kira  and his son now alive what the hell is  happening  this can't be a flashback his hair is  completely different the boy seems  driven to do something about his  situation too so  he seems to know what's going on kira  even meets him on his walk to school and  fills him in on more information before  leaving him and allowing rohan to  intercept the child  suddenly and without indication killer  queen jumps into the eye of rohan and  ultimately leads to his explosion  causing hayato  to relive that morning one hour in the  past  initially confusing the mechanics of  this new power of kira's become more and  more clear as time goes on while hayato  has experienced 